WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.890
Welcome to the Microsoft for Education Daily, Sunday edition.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.920
Here's what shipped at Microsoft in the last 24 hours.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.510
Back to class. Microsoft says Outlook,

00:00:17.510 --> 00:00:21.680
Teams and Copilot are fully restored after this week's outage.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:26.200
And watch for fake outage emails saying your held mail will be deleted.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:32.480
In Spain,

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:38.640
Valencia's Minecraft Education challenge now has a category for special education schools.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:43.580
In Rome on Tuesday, Microsoft's Elevate for Educators Day runs free,

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:45.800
hands-on AI workshops for teachers.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:47.780
Teaching online?

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:52.370
Teams is rolling out warnings that flag possible impersonators in your meetings.

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:54.770
From February,

00:00:54.770 --> 00:00:59.630
Teams' Facilitator should spot unanswered questions and offer to look them up.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:00.980
For school IT,

00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:06.530
an out-of-band update fixes November's bug that broke KMS activation commands.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.410
University dev teams on GitHub Enterprise Server ca

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:13.370
n now bring their repos into the GitHub Copilot app.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.390
Coding with Copilot?

00:01:16.390 --> 00:01:20.900
Google's Gemini 4 Hydrogen is rolling out, for Pro plans and up.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:26.550
Campus app makers get hourly alerts for critical flows,

00:01:26.550 --> 00:01:29.780
apps and agents, in preview by November 20.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:35.030
In the lab, a Microsoft researcher and an intern used AI to hunt for Linux bugs.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:43.640
Over 26,000 raw findings became 59 bug reports, after months of expert checking.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:51.560
On December 14, GitHub Copilot retires six models, like Gemini 3.8 Flash.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:55.300
And if your school's IT support uses ScreenConnect,

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:58.260
Microsoft says attackers abused it to spread malware.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:06.320
After hours, Candy Crush celebrates Xbox's 25th with Halo,

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:09.390
Fallout and Forza pins, for four weeks.

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:12.460
Six game themes got the Candy Crush treatment,

00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:15.870
with an orchestra, a choir and, yes, an accordion.

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:17.960
And from Tuesday,

00:02:17.960 --> 00:02:23.080
Ranger's Path lets you restore trails and document wildlife in a national park.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:29.570
Services restored, fakes spotted, fixes in: Monday's sorted. Back to class.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.820
Every day, the changelog gets a little longer.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.690
On the release board: shipped, and still shipping.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.410
That was 24 hours at Microsoft. Tomorrow, there's more.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.950
That's the Microsoft for Education Daily for today.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.310
Stay curious. See you tomorrow.
